From 5c63e34df9238de9d3aaeb750980853441aae5e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:45:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Screens drawn by code (API 56, capability screen): the
 screens.wasm component, a command buffer per frame, host fields

A menu type whose screen says "code": true is drawn by its mod's screens.wasm (world horizon-screen-mod), run in the
player's game: open/tick/render/input/close; render returns one command buffer (FILL, GRADIENT, BLIT, SPRITE,
NINE as Mekanism's blitNineSlicedSized, TEXT, ITEM, FLUID, SCISSOR, pose, SLOTS/SLOT, AREA, FIELD, TOOLTIP; 8192
commands, 256 KiB). The game renders only when something changed (tick, input, another area under the cursor) or
the frame animates, and draws the last buffer otherwise. screen-host reads the synchronised menu (data, strings,
grid, slots, carried, text width, texture size, translate) and sends through the menu's paths (button, menu_text,
grid click, click sound, close). Text fields are the game's (EditBox, touch keyboard, IME; type --menu-field).

- horizon-mod-sdk: screen module (ScreenMod, export_screen_mod!, Canvas in screen_format.rs, host), widgets after
  Mekanism's GuiScrollList, GuiScrollBar, GuiWindow and side tabs; example screen-demo with screens/.
- horizon-mods: screen_runtime (fuel, memory, imports limited to log and screen-host), Package reads screens.wasm,
  capability screen, API 56; [[screen]] steps in tests/*.toml; examples/screen_bench.
- cargo-horizon-mod: builds screens/ into screens.wasm.
- client: code_screens.rs (draw before and after the slots, input, fields, slots, tooltip), horizon-ctl ui lists
  screen-ID areas and screen_commands, state has screen_code (render times, fps with the screen open).
- agent_control_e2e.py --scenario screen; docs/mods-screen.md.
Also: the game's tests compile with the mods feature again (two `mod tests` in game/mods.rs).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
